<div class="home-grid">

  <section class="about-site">
    <p class="label">What this site is</p>
    <p>
      This is my public notebook. I learn by building and explaining, and
      everything that produces ends up here.
    </p>
    <p>
      The <a href="/blog/"><strong>blog</strong></a> holds long-form series you
      read like chapters, the biggest being the mathematics ML runs on, built
      from the silicon up. <a href="/courses/"><strong>Courses</strong></a>
      carries the slides and material from courses I teach, like computer
      organisation and design. <a href="/projects/"><strong>Projects</strong></a>
      is the maker log: embedded systems, TinyML experiments, things that worked
      and things that did not. <a href="/papers/"><strong>Papers</strong></a> is
      the newest thread, short honest reviews of what I am reading. And
      <a href="/culti7/"><strong>Culti7</strong></a> is the one finished thing
      among the works-in-progress: a moisture meter for cashew processors,
      in the field since 2021.
    </p>
    <p>
      Most of this is in progress. Some of it is wrong on the first try.
      I fix it as I learn better.
    </p>
    <p class="say-hello">
      If you work on similar things, I would genuinely love to hear from you
      &mdash; <a href="mailto:amdadithya@gmail.com">amdadithya@gmail.com</a>
    </p>
  </section>

  <aside class="interests">
    <p class="label">Currently interested in</p>
    <ul>
      <li>making neural nets fit in kilobytes</li>
      <li>how machines actually count</li>
      <li>the math underneath ML</li>
      <li>building things that survive the field</li>
      <li>teaching without hand-waving</li>
    </ul>
  </aside>

